  "currentRoundInspection": {
    "inspectedOn": "2026-10-15",
    "scope": "Four actually inspected exterior pictures and standard viewer PMTiles/DEM. No bespoke plans/surveys researched or reference photos redistributed. Rear-detail date unspecified and spire tip cropped in elevated view; fine current finish and all heights remain approximate.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gen%C3%A8ve_Cath%C3%A9drale_St._Pierre_Fassade.JPG",
        "author": "Zairon",
        "date": "2013-01-12",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected frontal photograph. Six free-standing pale Corinthian columns support deep horizontal entablature and triangular pediment; broad steps reach a recessed central brown rectangular portal and upper rectangular glazing. Shallow rounded gray barrel-like roof rises behind the pediment. Adjacent south Maccabees chapel has tall pointed traceried front glazing, massive buttress corners and steep triangular gable with cross and small crest; exact carving unresolved."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Pierre_Cathedral_-_Geneva,_Switzerland_-_panoramio.jpg",
        "author": "Sergey Ashmarin",
        "date": "2014-08-21",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected southwest oblique photograph. Six-column portico stands beside the tall Maccabees chapel; chapel has tan coursed walls, stepped projecting buttresses, tiled steep roof, selected narrow upper lights and large pointed windows. Beyond it, pale south tower has three actual open round belfry arches on each visible face, dark brown hipped/pyramid roof, small dormers/corner finials and weather vane. Very tall narrow oxidized green central spire rises behind."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parte_absidale_della_Cattedrale_di_San_Pietro_a_Ginevra.jpg",
        "author": "André Corboz / Iconotheque of the Academy of Architecture",
        "date": null,
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected older color rear-detail photograph; date unspecified. Faceted rounded east apse has a steep brown tiled hipped roof with green ribs, tall round-headed recessed windows and stepped stone buttresses. Lower neighboring roofs/chimneys are separate host buildings. Photo supports broad surviving forms, not current finish. Fine window tracery and roof patina simplified."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cathedral_of_Geneva.jpg",
        "author": "Bernard Vogel",
        "date": "2020-03-15",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected elevated eastern overview. South tower has broad brown pyramidal roof/dormers and a three-arched open stage; north tower differs with two three-arched open upper stages/balustrade, tall narrow steep tiled roof and flanking stone pinnacles. Between towers a tall green octagonal spire has a panelled/louvered lower shaft, slender ribs and small surrounding pinnacles. Brown steep main/cross/apse roofs carry green ridges; apse is polygonally rounded. Spire tip cropped by photograph; overall height remains estimated."
      }
    ]
  }
}
